t is. It shows you are polite and demonstrates your interest in the position.   <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Kristi</span>:  Really? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Adam</span>: Yes.  According to a survey I read, 75% of interviewers said that receiving a thank you letter from a candidate affects their decision-making process.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Kristi</span>: When should you send it?", "id": 2}, {"time": "33300", "image": "engenn9le13ob08re2img07.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Adam</span>: They said a thank you letter was best sent by e-mail within 24 hours of the interview, while they're still thinking about you. That's why I'm sending it this evening.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Kristi</span>:  I have an interview next week. I'll write one too.  Go ahead.<br>", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "14900", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\"> Why should you write a thank you note?</span>", "id": 1}, {"time": "33900", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\"> What do you include in a thank you note?</span>", "id": 2}], "video_src": "engenn9le13ob08re3vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Dressing the Part"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Thank You Note"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reported Speech and Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use<span class=\"strong\"> reported speech</span> when you are saying (reporting)  what other people have said or asked."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you tell people what someone has said in the past, you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past'. You need to change the verb to the next past form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'m coming</span> to the party.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming</span>. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had already</span> eaten.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to <span class=\"strong\">report questions</span> asked and the question is a yes/no questions, you use <span class=\"strong\">if</span> or <span class=\"strong\">whether</span> to report it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">They asked me <span class=\"strong\">if/whether</span> I wanted a job with benefits."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For a sentence in the future tense using <span class=\"strong\">will</span>, you use <span class=\"strong\">would</span> in<span class=\"strong\"> reported speech</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of <span class=\"strong\">reported speech and questions</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Statement/Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We are looking for an employee who is a strong leader. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You mentioned you were looking for an employee who was  a strong team player.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We want someone dynamic and self-motivated.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You said you wanted someone who was  dynamic and self-motivated.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you want a job with benefits?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They asked me if I wanted a job with benefits. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I will come to the meeting.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he would come to the meeting.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future with Will, Going to, the Present Continuous and the Simple Present Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use four different tenses to talk about the future. Each of them has their own use and structure. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the modal <span class=\"strong\">will </span> when you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Sure I'<span class=\"strong\">ll </span> read it and let you know what I think.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">be going to </span> when you ask or talk about intentions.  <br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">m going to</span> send a thank you letter.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Continuous tense </span> when you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future.  <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">That's why I'<span class=\"strong\">m sending</span> it this evening.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present </span> when you talk about schedules.  <br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">have</span> an interview next week.</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "interviewer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person in a company who gives an interview"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: According to a survey I read, 75% of interviewers said that receiving a thank you letter from a candidate affects their decision-making process."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you write a thank-you note."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hiring expert "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who knows a great deal about how to get a job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, according to a lot of hiring experts, it is."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "survey"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a series of answers to questions that are compiled to give an overall view of a situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: According to a survey I read, 75% of interviewers said that receiving a thank you letter from a candidate affects their decision-making process."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "your utmost satisfaction "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " in a manner that you are completely happy with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope I was able to answer all of your questions to your utmost satisfaction."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "do not hesitate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feel free or at ease to do something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As we discussed, I believe my writing style and my ability to manage an editorial calendar will serve me well in tracking down great stories for Never Odd Or Even."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le13ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online. Find 5 sample thank you notes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the notes. Look up any new words you do not know."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, discuss which is the best thank you note. Does it follow the correct structure? Does it use formal language? It is clear polite?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Put the thank you notes in order from #1 (best) to #5 (worst)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss ways the worse thank you note (#5) could be improved."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read a variety of thank you notes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the structure and quality of thank you notes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I suggest possible improvements to thank you notes."}]}]}